    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0269" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/2008: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-16T00:00:00-04:00">August 16,
                        1937—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>237. From Hornbeck.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d256-f1"/> Your 495, August 16, 4 p.m.
                    Paragraphs 1, 3 and all: you have my sympathy.</p>
                <p>Paragraphs 2, 4, 5, 6: I am sure action will be approved.</p>
                <p>Paragraph 7, second sentence: Steps have been initiated to provide funds to cover
                    emergencies.</p>
                <p>I understand that Navy Department has sent message to Commander in Chief which I
                    trust will be good news to both Commander in Chief and you. [Hornbeck.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="51" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>Stanley K. Hornbeck, Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
